{
  "issue_gist": "SimplexTableau's basic-variable detection treated any nonzero entry in a column as indicating a basic variable, rather than requiring the entry to equal exactly 1 (with the rest of the column zero). This misidentifies non-basic columns as basic and produces wrong solutions.",
  "concrete_examples": [
    {
      "input": "A tableau column for a variable contains a single nonzero entry that is not 1 (e.g. 2 or -1) and zeros elsewhere, so the variable is not basic, e.g. a column [0, 2, 0] in the constraint rows.",
      "expected": "The variable is not treated as basic. Its value is 0, and the basic variable is only recognized when the lone nonzero entry equals 1.",
      "actual": "The variable is treated as basic because its entry is nonzero. The solution reads its value from the RHS (possibly divided incorrectly or not at all), so the reported solution is wrong."
    }
  ]
}

